def table(headers,rows):
    # Last item in each row is a list of official references. Empty cells remain empty.
    out='<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th scope="col">'+e(h)+'</th>' for h in headers+['Official source / scope'])+'</tr></thead><tbody>'
    for row in rows:
        *cells,refs=row
        assert refs
        out+='<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(str(c))+'</td>' for c in cells)+'<td>'+''.join(f'<a href="{e(S[s][1])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e(S[s][0])} ↗</a>' for s in refs)+'</td></tr>'
    return out+'</tbody></table></div>'
def section(title,text,headers,rows):
    return '<section><h2>'+e(title)+'</h2><p>'+e(text)+'</p>'+table(headers,rows)+'</section>'
P['index.html']=('Overview','Make the decision.\nNot the assumptions.','An evidence-first framework for inherited property, housing choices, and long-term wealth.',
'''<div class="metrics"><article><span>FEDERAL EXCLUSION · 2026</span><strong>$15,000,000</strong><p>Per decedent; gifts and filing rules matter. <a href="https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/estate-tax">IRS source ↗</a></p></article><article><span>PLANNING HORIZON</span><strong>2040–2050</strong><p>Future property values and tax thresholds are not verified forecasts.</p></article><article><span>PUBLIC DATA POLICY</span><strong>Private by design</strong><p>No personal records, property amounts, addresses, or account details are published.</p></article></div>'''+section('Executive summary','Recommendation: preserve flexibility. Do not commit now to a sale, rental conversion, or move based on an unverified future tax advantage. This is a planning framework, not an appraisal or individualized legal, tax, or investment advice.', ['Priority','Finding','Decision implication'],[
('01 · Property tax','Inherited basis and assessed value are different systems. A trust does not itself guarantee an assessment exclusion.','Establish eligibility before comparing live vs. rent.',['basis','faq']),
('02 · Housing choice','An eligible family home requires qualifying occupancy; value above the adjusted cap can still increase assessed value.','Living there is not automatically the cheapest option. Compare the tax savings against forgone net rent and housing costs.',['prop19','cap','faq']),
('03 · Sell & diversify','Inherited basis is generally date-of-death fair market value; gains above adjusted basis may be taxable.','A prompt sale can limit post-inheritance gains, but fees, debts and estate obligations still reduce proceeds.',['basis','estate']),
('04 · Portfolio context','Mixed personal/rental use requires appropriate expense allocation.','Compare the entire two-property portfolio; do not count unchanged rent as a benefit unique to one option. Analysis method, not a verified property result.',['rent']),
('05 · Estate liquidity','The federal exclusion applies to an estate and adjusted taxable gifts, not a separate allowance for each beneficiary.','Inventory all includible assets before calculating remaining headroom.',['estate']),
('06 · Evidence boundary','No independently verified property records or insurer quotes are available in this publication.','No reliable profit ranking or dollar forecast can be produced under the no-inference rule. See Flagged for Review.',['quote','basis'])]))
P['taxes.html']=('Tax & legal','Two tax systems.\nOne careful plan.','Current official rules, their limits, and the dates that matter.',section('Property tax rules','Figures displayed in dollars are rounded to the nearest $10. The linked authority controls: never use a rounded display as an exact filing threshold.', ['Topic','Verified rule','Application / limitation'],[
('Proposition 13','Generally 1% of assessed value plus voter-approved debt rates; annual base-year inflation adjustment capped at 2%.','This does not cap the entire tax bill at 1% or guarantee 2% growth every year. Direct charges and supplemental bills can differ.',['prop13']),
('Change of ownership','A nonexcluded ownership change generally resets value to current market value.','A trust transfer must be analyzed for the actual beneficial ownership change, exclusions and ownership shares.',['prop13','faq']),
('Proposition 19 eligibility','Qualifying transferor and transferee principal residence; parent-child or qualifying grandparent-grandchild relationship.','Do not assume all trust beneficiaries qualify. Nonresidential property does not receive this family-home exclusion.',['prop19','faq']),
('Adjusted exclusion · current window','$1,044,590 displayed; applies to transfers February 16, 2025–February 15, 2027.','Rounded display only. Adds to factored base-year value, not an unlimited freeze. Future amounts are blank.',['cap']),
('Eligible full-interest formula','New taxable value = B + max(0, M − B − C).','B = factored base-year value; M = transfer-date market value; C = applicable exclusion adjustment. Simplified full eligible transfer only; partial interests require allocation.',['faq']),
('Occupancy','Continual eligible principal-residence use is required to retain the family-home exclusion.','Do not assume moving in temporarily permanently preserves the assessment when later renting.',['faq']),
('Local bill','SF FY 2026–27 secured rate: 1.18162182%.','Not a rate for another county or a future year; direct charges may apply separately. No parcel-specific rate is verified.',['sftax']),
('Proposed change · not enacted here','LAO’s October 22, 2025 analysis of initiative 25-0017 describes restoring broader inherited-property exclusions, including certain non-primary property.','If enacted as analyzed, renting could become more favorable relative to occupying. Qualification, election outcome and current enactment status are unverified; this proposal is NOT used as current law.',['proposal']),
('Homeowners exemption','$7,000 assessed-value exemption; approximately $70 at the 1% base rate.','Must qualify; distinct from Proposition 19 exclusion.',['prop13'])])+section('Estate, inheritance & sale taxes','US-citizen/resident estate framework only. Citizenship, domicile, treaty, trust inclusion and generation-skipping transfer issues require individualized review.', ['Topic','Verified rule','What remains unknown'],[
('Federal estate filing · 2026','$15,000,000 basic exclusion / filing threshold framework.','Gross estate plus adjusted taxable gifts and specific exemption determine filing; deductions and credit determine actual tax.',['estate','706']),
('Portability','A surviving spouse may receive unused exclusion through a timely estate-return election.','Not automatic; marital status, prior returns and unused exclusion are unverified.',['estate']),
('California death taxes','No California estate return required for deaths on or after January 1, 2005. Historical inheritance tax applies to deaths before June 8, 1982.','Separate later income, gain and property taxes still matter. No local estate-tax threshold has been independently verified here; flagged for review.',['ca','ftb']),
('Inherited basis','Generally fair market value on death; alternate valuation only if properly elected.','Not every asset in every trust receives a basis adjustment. Trust inclusion and ownership require review.',['basis','estate']),
('Sale of primary home','Potential gain exclusion of $250,000, or $500,000 for eligible joint filers.','Ownership/use generally 2 of 5 years and other tests apply. Rental depreciation and nonqualified use can restrict relief.',['home']),
('Investment gains','Capital gains rates depend on income and asset type; additional net investment income tax may apply.','Future marginal tax rates and personal income are blank, not estimated.',['gains']),
('Post-inheritance income','California taxes income subsequently generated by inherited assets.','Do not treat rent, dividends, interest or retirement distributions as tax-free inherited cash.',['ftb'])]))
P['decision.html']=('Decision analysis','Compare the portfolio.\nThen choose the property.','A conditional decision framework—not an unsupported promise of maximum profit.',section('Live, rent, or sell','All methods below are analytical comparisons. Official links support the tax treatment, not the investment outcome. Actual rents, quotes, taxes and return assumptions are unverified; result fields are intentionally blank.', ['Option','Decision test','Key trade-off','Verified result'],[
('Live in Property A','Compare eligible tax savings + actual housing costs avoided against forgone after-tax rental income + incremental living/ownership cost.','Must satisfy and retain family-home eligibility. Do not assume existing housing costs are all avoidable.','',['faq','rent']),
('Rent Property A; use Property B for housing','Compare after-tax net rent and equity growth with an after-tax alternative portfolio on the same time horizon.','Model market-value reassessment if exclusion unavailable; vacancy, management, repairs, insurance, capital work and tenant rules matter.','',['prop13','rent','sfrent']),
('Sell Property A; reinvest','Investable proceeds = sale price − selling costs − debt payoff − sale taxes − retained estate obligations.','Use adjusted inherited basis, not historic purchase cost; avoid double-counting estate obligations. Returns and liquidity differ by asset.','',['basis','estate','gains']),
('Retain Property B as baseline','Include existing net cash flow in every scenario where it is unchanged; allocate owner vs rental use correctly.','Moving does not establish that rental revenue, unit legality or expenses remain unchanged.','',['rent','sfrent']),
('Savings / deposits','Compare after-tax interest and inflation-adjusted purchasing power; validate deposit coverage.','FDIC standard coverage is $250,000 per depositor, per insured bank, per ownership category. Stocks and mutual funds are not covered.','',['fdic','ftb'])])+section('Cash-flow and net-worth worksheet','Blank is not zero. No generic maintenance percentage, vacancy allowance, investment return or broker fee is silently substituted.', ['Measure','Calculation / treatment','Result'],[
('Rental operating cash flow','Collected rent − owner-paid utilities − tax − insurance − repairs − management − other operating cash costs. Subtract capital expenditures and debt service separately to get spendable cash.','',['rent']),
('Taxable rental income','Tax rules differ from cash flow: allocate expenses; depreciation is noncash, capital improvements may require capitalization, loan principal is not a rental deduction.','',['rent']),
('After-tax rental cash flow','Spendable cash − incremental income tax, calculated from an actual return including applicable loss limitations.','',['rent']),
('Terminal sale value','Market proceeds − selling costs − outstanding debt − applicable gain/recapture tax. Add accumulated after-tax cash flows consistently.','',['rent','gains']),
('Indifference test','Compare each scenario’s terminal after-tax net worth plus housing service on an identical horizon and risk basis. No supported inputs means no computed winner.','',['rent','basis','fdic']),
('Maximum profit vs risk','Diversification, liquidity, landlord effort and downside exposure must be assessed; highest projected return is not guaranteed profit.','',['fdic','gains'])]))
