P['inheritance.html']=('Inheritance steps','From trust\nto informed choice.','A practical sequence, with legal deadlines separated from planning actions.',section('Transfer workflow','This is a general checklist, not confirmation of the terms of any private trust. An attorney and fiduciary must determine the actual authority, beneficiaries, deadlines and tax treatment.', ['Step','When','Action / control'],[
('01 · Establish authority','Before distributing or selling','Privately review trust, recorded title, ownership fractions, successor trustee and whether property is included in the taxable estate. A trust label alone is not sufficient.',['estate','faq']),
('02 · Secure records and cash','Immediately after death · planning action','Obtain needed records, preserve insurance and reserve liquidity; inventory cash, securities, real estate, insurance and other includible assets without publishing them.',['estate','insurance']),
('03 · Trustee notifications','Generally within 60 days of triggering event','Serve required beneficiaries/heirs; vacancy and later-known-person exceptions affect timing. Counsel should verify the statutory notice and contest provisions.',['notice']),
('04 · Date-of-death valuation','At transfer valuation date','Obtain supportable fair market value and basis records; coordinate any alternate valuation election and basis consistency reporting.',['basis','706']),
('05 · Ownership statement','Generally within 150 days after death for nonprobate transfers','Trustee/transferee files in each relevant county. Probate cases use the inventory/appraisal filing timeline specified by statute.',['death']),
('06 · Residence choice','Within one year of transfer for exemption filing','If eligible and actually occupying the family home, apply for homeowners or disabled veterans exemption and submit Proposition 19 claim; claim generally within 3 years or before third-party transfer. Do not wait for trust administration to finish.',['prop19']),
('07 · Federal return and liquidity','Check death-year Form 706 deadline','Evaluate filing, available exclusion, prior gifts, spouse election, deductions and estate tax. Do not distribute funds needed for obligations.',['706','estate']),
('08 · Operating plan','After verifying occupancy and tax position','Get actual policy quotes, verify leases and units, allocate mixed-use costs, then calculate hold vs rent vs sell after tax.',['rent','insurance','sfrent']),
('09 · Distribute and monitor','As authorized by trust / advisers','Maintain basis and assessment records, account for income from inherited assets and revisit exclusion when occupancy changes. This checklist does not determine a distribution date.',['basis','faq','ftb'])]))
